  "body": "Right now, [`HIDDevice.forget()`](https://hid.spec.whatwg.org/#forget-method) does not do any state check before starting the forget operation.\n\nI propose that `forget()` should throw an `InvalidStateError` if the state is \"opening\" or \"closing\".\n\nThis prevents a similar racy situation like in #136:\n```js\nconst opening = device.open();\nawait device.forget();\n```\n\nNow the `close()` can finish before the `forget()`, and so the device can end up in an open state depending on which call wins the race. While this is less problematic for a `close()` followed by a `forget(), I think it makes sense to include the \"closing\" state in this for consistency.\n\nNote that Blink currently does this: [`HIDDevice.forget()` checks for whether a device change is in progress](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/modules/hid/hid_device.cc;l=317;drc=c9c5aa46178af92bcfcd7e54dbb14341c7cef37d) (which includes being in the middle of an `open()` call) and rejects the promise if so.",
